== Exercise 3 — Answer the Questions
1. *No.* Researchers believe it is a natural ability inherited from parents, not a learned skill, and less than 2% of the population has it.
2. They spend a lot of time working with *CCTV images* to identify criminals.
3. *No.* They can often identify people from seeing just *part of their face* (such as their eyes or nose).
4. He could *recognize the same actor in different movies* when watching them with his father.
5. It can be *hard to switch off* when not at work; he recognizes people constantly even when off duty.
6. He has had to *arrest people* when he is off duty (because he recognized them as criminals).

